WEBVTT

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:02.600
Abenon, Abenon.

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:04.730
Let's have a pillow fight.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:06.300
Nah.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.610
Come on.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:12.490
I told you he wouldn't.

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:14.700
Pillow fights are fun.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:16.620
Open the door.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:19.100
We got permission from Fuji-sensei.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:23.160
The owner of the inn even 
told us to go all-out.

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:26.220
They even provided us with 
pillows they didn't need.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:28.540
This is an official pillow fight!

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:32.100
Don't just hide in your room. Come on out!

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:34.010
It's open!

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:39.430
<i>The room was tragically surrendered 
when Fuzzy attempted to escape...</i>

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:41.580
Steady, steady...

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:42.850
Lucky!

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:45.980
I want to play, too, Haruitsuki!

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:48.360
Ready, and...

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:51.730
Fight!

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:57.240
Abeno, you're supposed to throw 
the pillow, not hit him with it!

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:01.170
This is a pillow <i>beating</i>!

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:37.460
<b>Mystery 7 "The Dabbler"</b>

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:43.930
Left.

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:47.210
Correct.

00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:48.720
Yes!

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:49.690
Feeling dizzy?

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:53.160
Nope. And I didn't have to 
hold my breath even once!

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:57.190
Well, I guess you pass?

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:58.690
All right!

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:03.450
What? He passes even though he got 
four out of ten questions wrong?

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:07.320
It's harder to sense if something's 
on the left or right up close

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:10.620
than vaguely sense the 
direction at a distance!

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:13.380
Ashiya, Abeno!

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:16.340
The bus home is here!

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:17.680
It's the bus!

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:20.800
Got it! We'll be right there!

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.020
Thanks!

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:26.350
Abeno-san. Yahiko and Fuzzy, too.

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:27.300
Huh?

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:33.400
Because of you guys, I've gotten better 
at detecting the presence of yokai.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:38.110
Thanks for helping me train 
for the past three days.

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:41.450
Are you okay now?

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:44.200
Yeah, I'm fine!

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:46.970
Then beginning tomorrow,

00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:50.830
you can start using your garbage 
detection abilities at work.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:51.960
Hunk of junk.

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:54.990
Line up, everyone.

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:57.880
<i>You're still calling me a hunk 
of junk even after I passed?</i>

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:01.220
Come in a little closer.

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:04.920
Ashiyan and Abenon, you guys 
didn't take any pictures?

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:08.680
Oh, yeah. We were kinda busy.

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:28.920
Later.

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:29.870
Bye.

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:30.660
Bye.

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:32.380
Bye-bye.

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:37.250
Hey.

00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:40.120
There's something inside.

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:52.730
It's hard to talk when you're so guarded.

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:56.300
Um, what did you want to talk about?

00:04:56.300 --> 00:05:00.310
Itsuki didn't give you my message?

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:01.320
What message?

00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:04.190
He wants to apologize.

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:05.970
Apologize?

00:05:05.970 --> 00:05:10.630
Itsuki and the Justice told me about 
what happened with the Executive.

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:18.000
That must've been a terrifying experience.

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:24.970
First, let me apologize for 
his rude behavior. Forgive us.

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:29.110
Uh... I'm fine now, really...

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:34.350
By the way, Ashiya-kun, do you like gambling?

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:37.450
Gambling?

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:41.610
I brought something to 
give you as an apology.

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:48.240
That's...

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:49.740
Itsuki.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:56.460
Mr. Legislator, what's inside those boxes?

00:05:56.880 --> 00:05:59.570
One is an empty, losing box.

00:05:59.570 --> 00:06:02.340
The other, the winning box, contains a prize.

00:06:03.310 --> 00:06:06.020
Losing and winning?

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:12.140
I actually made a bet with the Executive.

00:06:12.550 --> 00:06:15.270
If you choose the winning box,

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:19.270
he said he'd allow you to 
conditionally enter the Underworld.

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:20.310
What?

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:21.900
What?

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:25.680
You mean he'll undo my banishment?

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:26.700
Uh-huh.

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:30.280
Is that what the Executive said?

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:32.890
Of course. He said it himself.

00:06:32.890 --> 00:06:34.790
I had him sign an agreement, too.

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:36.490
Want to read it later?

00:06:37.190 --> 00:06:39.240
What did you do to the Executive?

00:06:43.190 --> 00:06:46.800
It's the natural result of his actions.

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:51.880
He attacked an employee of the Mononokean, 
an institution that serves me.

00:06:51.880 --> 00:06:54.700
Of course I'm not taking that lying down.

00:06:56.950 --> 00:06:59.480
<i>Sorry, Mr. Legislator.</i>

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:02.700
I'm forbidden from entering the Underworld?

00:07:03.930 --> 00:07:07.860
If you can promise you won't enter, 
the Executive says he won't harm you.

00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:13.490
<i>If being re-admitted means the 
Executive will come after me again,</i>

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:15.800
<i>I'd rather stay banished.</i>

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:16.810
<i>And besides...</i>

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:19.990
Will you protect another human?

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:22.380
Killing an employee is surely possible

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:26.460
for the master of the Mononokean,
since he's above the law.

00:07:27.810 --> 00:07:30.470
<i>It could have a negative effect on Abeno-san.</i>

00:07:34.630 --> 00:07:36.920
<i>It's better not to provoke him.</i>

00:07:37.510 --> 00:07:39.070
Um, Mr. Legislat—

00:07:39.070 --> 00:07:40.280
Hey, hunk of junk.

00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:41.190
Hunk of—

00:07:41.910 --> 00:07:42.810
Pick the winning box.

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:47.690
If you pick the losing box, 
I'm failing you all over again.

00:07:48.710 --> 00:07:51.450
<i>Hunk of junk... Failing...</i>

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:07.450
The "winning box," is it?

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:10.970
Right or left?

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:18.360
Um...

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:24.920
The left?

00:08:42.310 --> 00:08:43.910
Correct.

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:46.200
That voice...

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:48.890
Were you listening,

00:08:48.890 --> 00:08:50.500
<i>Justice?</i>

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:54.100
Yeah, I was listening.

00:09:03.220 --> 00:09:05.890
The Legislator won the bet.

00:09:08.820 --> 00:09:10.220
As promised,

00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:13.600
you're conditionally unbanished 
from the Underworld.

00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:16.250
I'll inform the Executive.

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:21.080
Conditionally?

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:24.200
What are the conditions?

00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:31.450
The Executive's condition is that

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:35.630
every time you enter the Underworld,

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:39.300
the Legislator has to go see the Executive 
and beg on his hands and knees.

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:48.310
How peculiar. That's not 
the condition I agreed to.

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:55.860
Personally, I'd recommend this one.

00:09:56.310 --> 00:09:59.200
Anyway, the actual condition is that

00:09:59.970 --> 00:10:03.290
Ashiya Hanae is only allowed to enter

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:06.600
when accompanied by myself.

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:08.650
By you?

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:16.460
And you're currently 
satisfying that condition.

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:19.720
There's no problem with you entering now.

00:10:20.930 --> 00:10:23.240
I'm falling, I'm falling!

00:10:26.050 --> 00:10:28.000
It's okay if you fall.

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:31.480
Or do you still not believe me?

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:33.820
No!

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:38.490
I'm grateful you got me
 re-admitted, but I...

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:46.040
I'm not entering the Underworld again.

00:10:47.780 --> 00:10:52.830
Tell the Executive I said that when you 
report the results of the bet to him.

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:54.920
I will.

00:10:56.550 --> 00:10:59.460
All that after he chose the winning box?

00:11:00.710 --> 00:11:04.470
But if that's his master's will, 
then I suppose it can't be helped.

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:09.130
I was thinking we could celebrate 
your re-admission here, but...

00:11:09.130 --> 00:11:09.980
What a shame.

00:11:12.310 --> 00:11:16.270
Celebrate? Do you have food?

00:11:16.270 --> 00:11:19.110
I have snacks to eat with sake.

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:22.870
<i>I picked the winning box like he told me to,</i>

00:11:22.870 --> 00:11:26.550
<i>but was picking the losing 
box the right choice?</i>

00:11:28.150 --> 00:11:30.000
Given what your master's saying,

00:11:30.950 --> 00:11:34.630
you may not have the opportunity 
to return to the Underworld again.

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:37.620
And judging by what I just saw,

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:41.740
you have some resistance to entering 
the Underworld yourself, right?

00:11:51.080 --> 00:11:52.620
I understand.

00:11:57.150 --> 00:12:00.900
When you decide to visit the Underworld,

00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:02.900
come see me.

00:12:04.450 --> 00:12:08.670
I have to accompany you so 
I can keep an eye on you.

00:12:08.670 --> 00:12:13.740
If I ever deem you a threat to the 
Underworld, I'll come after you.

00:12:15.220 --> 00:12:17.610
But as long as you're not,

00:12:17.610 --> 00:12:20.920
I'll protect you as an 
employee of the Mononokean.

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:27.360
<i>I'm still an uninvited guest.</i>

00:12:27.360 --> 00:12:32.540
<i>But a time may come when I choose to enter.</i>

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:43.500
When that time comes,

00:12:44.840 --> 00:12:46.700
I look forward to having your help.

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:57.210
Goodbye.

00:13:07.540 --> 00:13:11.150
Should I have chosen the 
losing box in the bet?

00:13:11.150 --> 00:13:11.920
What?

00:13:11.920 --> 00:13:15.900
I thought you might've preferred 
for me to stay banished.

00:13:15.900 --> 00:13:19.900
Oh. No, the winning box was right.

00:13:19.900 --> 00:13:20.730
In fact,

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:26.490
the Legislator put a yokai inside the 
winning box so you would pick it.

00:13:28.130 --> 00:13:32.890
The Legislator knew I learned to sense yokai?

00:13:32.890 --> 00:13:34.120
Probably.

00:13:34.430 --> 00:13:37.770
But I don't remember reporting 
that to the Legislator.

00:13:37.770 --> 00:13:40.270
Huh? Then how does he...

00:13:40.270 --> 00:13:44.710
Mononokean, you're the one who 
told the Legislator, aren't you?

00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:48.090
It's obvious you're feigning innocence!

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:53.100
Wait! Does that mean we just cheated 
the Executive and the Justice?

00:13:53.100 --> 00:13:55.740
Even for the Legislator, 
that's not a good idea!

00:13:55.740 --> 00:13:58.250
Especially if the Executive finds out...

00:13:58.250 --> 00:14:01.490
Don't worry about the Executive anymore.

00:14:01.490 --> 00:14:04.730
The Legislator seemed to have 
prepared himself for the worst.

00:14:04.730 --> 00:14:05.780
The worst?

00:14:06.470 --> 00:14:11.530
The Executive doesn't have time 
to further incur his wrath.

00:14:11.840 --> 00:14:13.210
His wrath?

00:14:13.210 --> 00:14:16.960
Was the Legislator that mad?

00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:21.170
He was sort of pleased that you 
picked the winning box, though.

00:14:23.320 --> 00:14:25.220
Are you satisfied now?

00:14:26.360 --> 00:14:28.080
Not at all.

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:31.680
I actually wanted to report to the Executive

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:37.680
that Ashiya-kun entered the 
Underworld, but Itsuki stopped him.

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:40.760
But you won the bet.

00:14:40.760 --> 00:14:44.830
I might feel better after 
seeing the Executive's face

00:14:44.830 --> 00:14:47.480
when he hears that he lost.

00:14:47.480 --> 00:14:50.600
I don't think the Executive will see you.

00:14:50.600 --> 00:14:52.120
Probably not.

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:54.700
The matter has been settled now.

00:14:58.840 --> 00:15:01.710
That should be the end of this infighting.

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:06.470
When you two fight, I always 
get caught in the middle.

00:15:07.220 --> 00:15:08.940
It's a pain in the butt.

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:13.830
It's because the Executive 
has a violent temper. But...

00:15:16.820 --> 00:15:21.730
Even someone as good-natured as 
myself won't let this one go.

00:15:23.730 --> 00:15:26.060
Good-natured, huh?

00:15:26.580 --> 00:15:28.040
If that were the case,

00:15:28.040 --> 00:15:31.860
I wouldn't have needed to get involved.

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:37.060
The next time you talk to the 
Executive, try to play nice.

00:15:40.690 --> 00:15:42.000
Well?

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:43.450
Fine.

00:15:43.860 --> 00:15:47.690
Justice, thanks for all your help.

00:15:48.800 --> 00:15:51.500
I'll treat you to something good to eat.

00:15:51.500 --> 00:15:54.010
Give my best to the Executive.

00:16:06.400 --> 00:16:07.880
Is that a ghost?!

00:16:08.370 --> 00:16:09.690
It's a raccoon dog.

00:16:12.160 --> 00:16:16.230
Zenko, slow down a little.

00:16:17.000 --> 00:16:20.760
Dad, that's the outlook at the peak.

00:16:43.570 --> 00:16:44.620
Zenko...

00:16:45.640 --> 00:16:48.190
Is that a ghost?

00:16:52.180 --> 00:16:53.700
Zenko...

00:16:53.700 --> 00:16:58.590
Are you sure there was a 
ghost at Outlook Ridge?

00:16:58.590 --> 00:17:03.490
Yes. It had long black hair 
and was wearing a white dress.

00:17:03.490 --> 00:17:05.830
It waved its hand at us, too.

00:17:06.390 --> 00:17:08.680
Its hand? You saw a hand?

00:17:09.490 --> 00:17:14.240
I see. I only saw its hair and 
clothing floating mid-air.

00:17:14.240 --> 00:17:17.190
It was just too dark for me to see its body.

00:17:19.400 --> 00:17:22.520
It could've been a prank played by some kids.

00:17:22.520 --> 00:17:26.140
<i>So Dad only saw its hair and clothes.</i>

00:17:27.860 --> 00:17:30.360
I'll call the president of 
the neighborhood association.

00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:31.310
You're calling him?

00:17:31.310 --> 00:17:35.680
He told me to call if I 
thought I saw a ghost.

00:17:35.680 --> 00:17:40.300
Depending on the situation, he said he 
might cancel the Bon Festival dance.

00:17:41.360 --> 00:17:44.090
Actually, a ghost caused quite 
a disturbance last year.

00:17:44.090 --> 00:17:46.920
There was a child who 
tripped and hurt herself.

00:17:47.520 --> 00:17:49.430
I see.

00:17:54.370 --> 00:17:56.130
That transparency...

00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:58.930
It was the same as how I see Fuzzy.

00:17:59.210 --> 00:18:02.920
It must've been a yokai and not a ghost.

00:18:02.920 --> 00:18:04.230
Hey, Zenko.

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:07.360
I remember now. Those guys...

00:18:07.360 --> 00:18:10.400
What guys? You mean a priest?

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:13.820
Abeno and... Ashida, was it?

00:18:14.160 --> 00:18:16.360
It's Ashiya, Dad.

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:20.320
They said they could sense and 
exorcise spirits, didn't they?

00:18:39.370 --> 00:18:40.180
It's here.

00:18:40.520 --> 00:18:42.360
You sense a yokai?

00:18:42.360 --> 00:18:43.180
Yup.

00:18:44.320 --> 00:18:48.780
Assuming my yokai radar 
can't sense ghosts, that is.

00:18:48.780 --> 00:18:50.940
Ghosts scare you in the middle of the day?

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:53.800
Do you want to wait for Abeno?

00:18:54.290 --> 00:18:56.240
He's still at work, right?

00:18:56.240 --> 00:18:59.630
No, I'm okay! Let's go!

00:18:59.630 --> 00:19:01.450
I sensed something this way!

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:06.460
You're making me lead?

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:17.630
<i>It noticed us?</i>

00:19:18.420 --> 00:19:21.590
<i>That's not a ghost, right?</i>

00:19:21.590 --> 00:19:24.390
<i>It's just a yokai, it's just 
a yokai, it's just a yokai...</i>

00:19:24.650 --> 00:19:27.320
<i>She's a yokai!</i>

00:19:28.080 --> 00:19:29.820
Nice to meet you!

00:19:29.820 --> 00:19:33.230
I'm Ashiya, an employee of the Mononokean!

00:19:33.640 --> 00:19:37.180
I was hired by a client to come look for you!

00:19:37.890 --> 00:19:41.060
You finally found me.

00:19:41.940 --> 00:19:46.300
Mononokean, make me human!

00:19:46.300 --> 00:19:47.280
Human?

00:19:47.280 --> 00:19:47.870
Why?

00:19:52.130 --> 00:19:55.170
Her head came off!

00:20:03.700 --> 00:20:05.300
Her hair came off, too...

00:20:05.300 --> 00:20:07.810
Don't pull off my hair!

00:20:18.840 --> 00:20:20.070
Welcome back.

00:20:20.070 --> 00:20:22.570
<b>Sitting                   Straight</b>

00:20:20.640 --> 00:20:22.570
<i>This is a bad sign.</i>

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:26.320
Um, about the ghost...

00:20:26.320 --> 00:20:28.810
It was a yokai after all.

00:20:29.430 --> 00:20:31.450
I brought her here.

00:20:33.110 --> 00:20:36.430
We gathered all the pieces.

00:20:36.430 --> 00:20:37.920
Is she conscious?

00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:38.840
I am.

00:20:39.560 --> 00:20:42.110
And this always happens.

00:20:42.110 --> 00:20:44.430
The pieces will stick together with water.

00:20:45.560 --> 00:20:47.920
My name is Keshi.

00:20:47.920 --> 00:20:51.100
I'm Abeno, master of the Mononokean.

00:20:51.680 --> 00:20:53.770
How long ago was it?

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:55.690
I ran into a yokai

00:20:55.690 --> 00:20:59.710
who told me there's a shop 
that grants wishes to yokai.

00:20:59.710 --> 00:21:04.540
I searched all over because
I had a wish I wanted granted.

00:21:04.540 --> 00:21:07.700
But no matter how much
I searched, I couldn't find it.

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:12.830
I put on human clothes and 
a wig so humans could see me

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:17.460
and caused disturbances by scaring them so 
the Mononokean would come find me instead.

00:21:18.040 --> 00:21:22.300
Apparently the hauntings have 
been happening since last year.

00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:24.900
She was responsible for all of them.

00:21:25.320 --> 00:21:28.510
Keshi-dono, what is the 
wish you want granted?

00:21:28.510 --> 00:21:31.630
For just one day, I want to become human

00:21:31.630 --> 00:21:35.270
and dance with them at 
the Bon Festival dance.

00:21:35.960 --> 00:21:37.180
The Bon Festival dance...

00:21:38.620 --> 00:21:43.310
But the Mononokean can't 
turn yokai into humans.

00:21:43.310 --> 00:21:45.500
That's what Ashiya-dono told me.

00:21:46.040 --> 00:21:50.170
So I want you to disguise 
me to look human enough

00:21:50.170 --> 00:21:54.010
that I won't scare the other humans.

00:23:25.040 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Next Time: "The Removal"</b>

00:23:25.890 --> 00:23:29.550
Granting the yokai her wish 
seems like it'll be difficult,

00:23:29.840 --> 00:23:33.930
but it might be easier than making 
my dad remember Ashiya's name.

00:23:34.610 --> 00:23:36.260
Next time, "The Removal."

00:23:36.260 --> 00:23:38.980
And besides, it's kind of fun.
